`GetType()` is called once and stored in a local, instead of up to three times. It is likely a virtual call. The `IsValid()` check stays first, as in the original. This assumes `GetType()` is a side-effect-free const getter, so calling it once returns the same value the repeated calls did.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
        return (FIT_UINT8)(values.size() / baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK]);

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```